ID: B3-Ch08a-Rescue
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch4_billy <= 6 && v_b3_ch4_billy != 7 && v_b3_ch4_billy != 8 || v_b3_ch4_billy == 9) {
"I'm on whichever side helps us rescue the prisoners from the seredium towers."

"Contradiction," the Overseer says. "Neither faction will designate the liberation of seredium tower captives as an objective. Clarify your target."

"Why wouldn't the rebels free their own comrades?" I ask.

"The tower inmates power the city's infrastructure," the Overseer says. "Extracting the captive mages collapses the power grid, disabling levitation transports and automated municipal devices across Ollendor. The resulting municipal paralysis will cost civilian lives. The underground king understands this balance and will maintain the siphon until alternate energy conduits are secured."

"Then I stand with neither of you," I say. "If keeping people chained in batteries is the plan, both factions are hostile."

"Easy, Barry," Daren says, stepping in. "We have not discussed this with the underground king yet. He has proven practical so far. We can negotiate a compromise that frees the prisoners without violence."

"The underground king's pragmatism does not extend to compromise on this point," the Overseer says.

"What makes you certain?" Daren asks.

"One hour ago, this crystal captured a direct exchange between the underground king and his lieutenant," the Overseer says. "The orders were explicit regarding the elimination of your unit if you oppose his coronation. Listen."

}
#if(v_b3_ch4_billy == 7 || v_b3_ch4_billy == 8) {
"I'm on whichever side helps us rescue the prisoners from the seredium towers."

"Given that our preliminary accord establishes the liberation of prisoners as a primary objective," the Overseer says, "this confirms your allegiance to my administration."

"If that holds," I say.

