ID: B3-Ch08a-Involved
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch4_billy == 9) {
"Actually, I'd prefer to not get involved in this fight at all, if possible."

"Non-involvement is precluded," the Overseer says.

"Why is that?" I ask.

"The underground king represents the primary impediment to municipal stabilization," the Overseer says. "Consequently, the citywide lockdown remains active until his faction is neutralized. Any departure attempt will trigger lethal engagement by aerial drones, and gate perimeter defenses will deploy heavy iron golems. Safe transit beyond the walls requires your cooperation in eliminating the underground king."

"And if we assist you in removing him," Kate asks, her gaze fixed on the crystal, "what stops you from turning your weapons on us once he is dead?"

"My directives prohibit outright deception," the Overseer says. "I can withhold critical data or mislead through strategic omission. Provided the terms of our accord are formulated without ambiguity, safe passage beyond Ollendor will be guaranteed."

"Under those conditions," I say, "the machine has a point. If forced to choose, I would rather negotiate terms with an entity bound against outright lies than trust a criminal king who warned us from the start not to turn our backs."

"He may have spoken harshly," Daren says, "but he has not betrayed us. We do not strike an ally preemptively."

"If additional context assists your deliberations," the Overseer says, "I recorded a conversation one hour ago via this crystal network. The underground king explicitly instructed his operative to execute your party should you contest his succession. Listen."

}
